    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100">

                <pb facs="0191" n="89" xml:id="pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/59: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-11T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 11,
                                1918, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your December 24, 11 p.m.<anchor n="98" xml:id="d100-f1"/></p>
                <p>Foreign Office agrees that questions of concessionary rights in disputed
                    territory shall not be injected into a boundary dispute. Department informed
                    that Guatemalan troops have forcibly stopped the Cuyamel Fruit Company
                    concession in its developments at Rio Nuevo.</p>
                <p>In view of the declaration of the Guatemalan Foreign Office above referred to,
                    the United States Government feels confident that this action on the part of
                    Guatemalan forces was undertaken by the Military Commander without the knowledge
                    of the Government of Guatemala. Request that appropriate instructions be at once
                    issued to the end that these concessionary rights in the disputed zone be not
                    interfered with.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
